#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101607} :activity/id #uuid "e442df57-09a3-5dc2-8ca2-459fbbe7227c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050961 :topic/id #uuid "75a8462b-b2e3-545e-a142-3221dfd27093" :topic/math-academy-id 1249} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101607 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101942 :tutorial/content "Let's suppose we only know the values of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ at $x=0$ along with their derivatives, as given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n\nCan we calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big )$ at $x=0?$\n\nUsing the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) = f'(x)g(x)+f(x)g'(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\left.\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) \\right|_{x=0}\t=\tf'(0)g(0)+f(0)g'(0).\n$$\n\nAll of these values are given in the table! So, substituting the values from the table into the formula, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & ={f}^{'}(0)g(0)+f(0){g}^{'}(0) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "9df0b4fa-df54-5f34-9bdc-3fc11befd2e8" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2627 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "060c1ce4-0c9d-5214-85ce-1b51fedd7791" :step/math-academy-id 12338 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101756}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101608 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100662 :question/id #uuid "0713e68d-2b3e-5010-954f-7891d96bdbbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3640"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048842}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101218} {:db/id